IAM + AWS SERVICES
------------------

21. How does Sync-Service access AWS services securely?
- Use IAM-based workload identity.
- EKS Pod Identity / IRSA.
- Assign required IAM permissions to workload.
- Avoid hardcoded AWS credentials.

Sync-Service Pod
       ↓
IAM Role
       ↓
AWS S3 / DynamoDB / Secrets Manager


22. Why shouldn't AWS access keys be put inside Pods?
Long-lived credentials can leak through:
- Git
- Docker image
- Logs
- Kubernetes YAML
- Developer machines

Use temporary credentials through workload identity.

23. Sync-Service only needs S3 read access. What permissions?
- Grant only required S3 read permissions.
- Restrict to required bucket/object.

Follow Least Privilege.

Don't give AdministratorAccess.

